    {
      "id": "ledger-notes",
      "kind": {
        "text": "The proof needs no sign analysis, and that is the content: `Int.mul` sends BOTH same-sign branches into `Int.ofNat` -- `ofNat m * ofNat m` is `ofNat (m*m)` and `negSucc m * negSucc m` is `ofNat (succ m * succ m)` -- and a square is always same-sign. So neither branch of the `Int.rec` split has a hypothesis to use or to refute, and both close with `Nat.zero_le` at the magnitude the branch produced. `formal.statement` is `Kernel::render_lean` of the admitted type, verbatim from `int_theorem_inventory`.",
        "type": "prose"
      },
      "provenance": {
        "command": "python3 render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
        "epoch": {
          "commit": "d637d83f77dbfa43c98eee4ab0ad78d235099006",
          "source": "commit",
          "unix": 1787144076
        },
        "exit_status": 0,
        "generator": "render/producers-py/facts_to_docir.py",
